---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="About — Fiction & Fact Library">
  <section class="hero wrap" style="padding-bottom: 8px;">
    <p class="eyebrow">Colophon</p>
    <h1>About this <em>reading room</em></h1>
    <div class="ornament"><span>❧</span></div>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap" style="max-width: 740px;">
    <p class="book__desc" style="max-width: none;">
      <b>Fiction &amp; Fact Library</b> is a small, lovingly-typeset web player for the world’s
      public-domain audiobooks. Every recording here was read aloud by a volunteer at
      <a href="https://librivox.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LibriVox</a>, whose mission is to
      record every book in the public domain. The accompanying texts come from
      <a href="https://www.gutenberg.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Project Gutenberg</a>.
    </p>
    <p class="book__desc" style="max-width: none;">
      The catalogue is fetched live from the
      <a href="https://archive.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Internet Archive</a>’s
      <code>librivoxaudio</code> collection, which mirrors LibriVox and exposes a fast,
      CORS-friendly search API. That means this entire site is <i>completely client-side</i>:
      there is no server, no database, and no tracking. The pages are static HTML; the books
      stream straight from the Archive to your browser.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin-top: 32px;">Your data stays yours</h2>
    <p class="book__desc" style="max-width: none;">
      Favorites and listening progress are stored in your browser’s <code>localStorage</code>.
      They never leave this device and are never sent anywhere. Clear your browser data and they’re gone.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin-top: 32px;">A note on the name</h2>
    <p class="book__desc" style="max-width: none;">
      The public domain holds more than novels. Alongside <i>fiction</i> — the great stories,
      adventures and romances — sits a vast shelf of <i>fact</i>: history, philosophy, science,
      memoir and essays. The <b>Fiction &amp; Fact Library</b> gathers both, so an afternoon can
      drift from <i>Sherlock Holmes</i> to <i>The Art of War</i> without leaving your chair.
    </p>

    <div class="ornament" style="margin-top: 36px;"><span>✦ ✦ ✦</span></div>
    <p class="center" style="margin-top: 18px;">
      <a class="btn" href={import.meta.env.BASE_URL}>Enter the library →</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
